WEBVTT

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.240
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.150
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.900
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.600
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.700
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.070
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:46.000
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.250
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:59.520
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:06.260
What is truly precious?

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:13.320
It is her!  Rebecca, you're...

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.760
You finally realized.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.690
Yes, my name is Rebecca Hopkins.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:27.170
I'm the granddaughter of Arthur Hopkins, and you stole his precious Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.870
You're my grandpa's best friend's granddaughter?

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.500
That's right.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:38.250
I'll make you feel every bit of my grandfather's resentment.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.180
Prepare yourself!

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:46.180
Deadly Shadow Ghoul

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:55.990
My grandpa would never steal someone else's card!

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.330
No!

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.980
He stole it!

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:04.520
My grandpa cherished that card.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:08.320
I won't forgive you!

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:10.210
Rebecca.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:11.480
What is it?

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.700
Can I tell you a story about my friend?

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.590
It's about my dear friend - your grandfather Arthur Hopkins.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.110
You're just gonna make excuses!

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.330
I don't want to hear it!

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:30.420
Rebecca, since you're Arthur's granddaughter, you must hear this story.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:37.130
It happened several years ago when I traveled to Egypt.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:45.180
I was very interested in Duel Monsters, though few knew about it back then.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:53.780
I heard rumors that there were extremely rare cards in Egypt.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.790
So I went all the way over there.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:59.790
That's where I met him.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.400
Feel free to drink my water.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.200
Thank you.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.480
Arthur was excavating archeological sites.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.440
Despite his age, he smiled like a child.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.310
He was a wonderful man.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:23.910
But in the archaeological world, he was seen as an outsider.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.420
Why?

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:31.870
Because he was very interested in Duel Monsters, just like me.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.590
Isn't that right, Rebecca?

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.980
What do you mean, Grandpa?

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:43.970
While examining the writing at the ruins, he noticed that a particular word kept popping up.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.900
The word was...

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:47.270
"Game."

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.210
Game?

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.640
Game?

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.300
Yes.  Game.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:01.740
With that keyword, he reevaluated his analysis of ancient Egyptian text.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.620
And he reached an unbelievable conclusion.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.790
This is what's written here:

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:14.730
“By order of the sun god, exchange the cards that fortell the great Pharaoh's future."

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.670
Exchange the cards?

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.480
Correct.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.110
They frequently performed ceremonies to foretell the future of the Pharaoh and his people.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.440
It involved exchanging cards.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.350
In other words, a game.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:29.950
What?

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:33.060
Yes, they played a card game.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:35.600
Look at this.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.560
Those are Duel Monsters.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:43.430
This is where they got their inspiration.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.770
It's the same picture as the card game.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:49.640
I think ancient Egyptians also played this game.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.710
This is an incredible discovery.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:56.920
When you present this to the academic world, Egyptologists will be shocked.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.330
Well...

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:05.970
But in the archaeological world, Arthur's theories were laughed at.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:13.990
He never gave up and excavated more sites to find evidence that would prove his theories.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:18.360
I thought his theories were exciting and found a kindred spirit.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:22.300
He also proposed the existence of God Cards.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.050
God Cards?

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.200
There are several God Cards in the world.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.250
When all these cards are gathered, they will transform into the sun god...

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:35.300
...and the owner will become king of the world.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:36.650
King of the world?

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:41.030
According to this prophecy, when the cards gather at a single location...

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:44.910
...the owner gains the power to rule the world.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:51.330
But the riddle of the God Cards won't be solved easily.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.330
I intend to spend the rest of my life researching it.

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:58.440
God Cards?

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:03.540
You received Blue-Eyes White Dragon from Professor Hopkins?

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:04.720
That's right.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:05.810
Liar!

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.800
Lies!  Lies!  Lies!

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.910
You stole my grandpa's card at that time!

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.330
That's what happened!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.280
Right, Teddy?

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.310
Rebecca.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:21.910
Rebecca, that's when the ruins collapsed around us.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:24.960
Collapsed?

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.280
Are you okay, Sugoroku?

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.510
Yes, I'm fine.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.930
However...

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:39.660
This is bad.  We're trapped inside.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:46.380
No rescue teams arrived.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:55.390
We ran out of food, and we were only left with enough water for one person.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.160
That's when...

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.180
Sugoroku.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.100
What is it?

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.030
Want to play a game?

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:07.770
We can't give up hope, but just in case.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:11.410
Let's play a game while we leave the rest to fate.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.080
You're right.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:17.310
Professor Hopkins, I have an idea.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.450
What is it?

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:21.220
There's only a small amount of water left.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:27.900
But one of us will have to drink it in order to prolong his life.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:32.750
How about the winner of this duel drinks the rest of the water?

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.160
That's fine.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.830
All right, let's duel!

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:42.880
On the first turn of the duel, Arthur played Witch of the Black Forest.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.680
Witch of the Black Forest.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:49.550
That's right.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:52.980
You learned your strategy from Arthur, didn't you?

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.990
What happened in the end?

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.440
Well...

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.080
I don't want to hear it!

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:03.220
There's no proof that you're telling the truth!

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:05.110
That's not a nice thing to say!

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:08.430
It's my turn.

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:12.140
Hey!  Grandpa hasn't finished his story yet!

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:14.080
No, let her continue.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.510
Continue, you two.

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:23.880
Goddamn!  You're the one who interrupted us in the first place!

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:29.680
It's strange.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:34.290
It feels like Arthur himself is in that Ring.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.230
Okay, I'll play this.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:41.700
Catapult Turtle in attack position!

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:53.090
Catapult Turtle lets me tribute a monster and deal half its attack points as damage.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.550
So what?

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:58.780
Next, I use the spell card Brain Control.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.710
What?  I don't like that!

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:05.890
I take control of your monster and use it as my own for one turn.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.600
Come, Millennium Shield!

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:16.580
Then I use Catapult Turtle to launch Millennium Shield.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:22.070
Oh no!

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:24.860
My turn isn't over yet.

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:25.950
Battle!

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:33.250
Cannon Soldier is destroyed!

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.690
How frustrating!

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:38.660
Nice, Yugi!

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:41.390
You did it, Yugi!  Keep it up!

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.090
Impressive, Yugi Muto.

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:04.080
I can see why he's the winner of Duelist Kingdom.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:12.420
I have six monsters in my graveyard.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.970
But that's not enough.

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:22.000
Great!  Fantastic!

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.900
We did it, Teddy!

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.160
Bravo!

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:26.370
What's with her?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.370
V!  I won!

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:32.910
The spell card Judgment Blaster!

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:34.280
What?

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:38.280
By discarding five cards from my hand...

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.040
In exchange...

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.330
All monsters on the field are destroyed!

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:55.000
Next, I summon Shadow Ghoul in attack position.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:03.940
My favorite monster, Shadow Ghoul, has arrived!

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:10.210
It gains 100 attack points for each monster that went to my graveyard.

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:12.310
For each one?

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.620
How many monsters are in her graveyard?

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:17.260
Eleven!

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.900
One hundred times eleven is...  Umm...

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:20.930
1100.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:25.130
How's that!  Shadow Ghoul now has 2700 attack points.

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:32.330
You were sending your monsters to the graveyard to power up Shadow Ghoul.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.400
Of course.  You just realized that now?

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:37.140
You're a slow one.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:38.880
Rebecca.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.570
What?

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.980
In a duel, your heart has to believe in your cards.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:48.920
It's cruel to send your monsters to the graveyard simply to power it up.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.280
You're such an idiot!

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:54.620
You're naive if you think dueling has anything to do with heart.

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:58.130
A duelist does whatever it takes to win!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:02.900
Don't make up stories to hide the fact that you stole the card!

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:06.120
I learned these tactics from my grandfather too.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:11.320
Monsters are only good as weapons or sacrifices!

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:13.240
Are you sure?

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:20.680
Grandpa, I sort of understand how the duel in the ruins ended.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:25.020
Yugi, keep dueling the way you like.

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.920
I understand, Grandpa.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:30.620
Hey!  How long are you going to keep a lady waiting?

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:32.060
Hurry up, Yugi!

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:36.100
I set a monster in defense position.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:46.470
Yugi, did you know that the luck of the draw comes from skill?

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.510
The spell card Stop Defense.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.320
Shadow Ghoul attacks!

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.320
Tears of Cemetery!

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.030
Bye bye, Dark Magician.

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:12.450
Grandpa, can't anything be done?

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:14.620
You remember your old duel, right?

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:15.450
Yes.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:16.400
In that case...

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.570
Just keep watching.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:21.510
This duel will end one way or another.

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:24.020
Swords of Revealing Light!

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:28.180
It stops your Battle Phase for three turns.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.780
You're desperate.  How annoying.

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:33.490
I'll pass this turn.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:35.760
She's acting like nothing bothers her.

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:38.120
I play this.

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:40.180
Monster Reborn.

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:43.360
I resurrect Dark Magician.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:49.220
I see.  You're gathering your attack pieces while I can't do anything.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.520
But it won't work.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:53.770
I'll win anyway.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:56.640
I play my next card in defense, but I'll tell you what it is.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.580
It's Cannon Soldier.

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:03.220
She's trying to get me to attack.

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:06.060
But I can't let her keep Cannon Soldier.

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:08.660
I have no choice!  I attack Cannon Soldier!

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.600
Black Magic!

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:20.570
Shadow Ghoul gains 100 attack points again.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:27.980
I think Yugi is waiting for a certain card.

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:29.240
A certain card?

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.340
Yeah.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.810
I'm sure he'll make a big comeback in the end!

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.300
Your strategy is obvious.

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:40.240
You're using Swords of Revealing Light to stall for time, waiting to get a certain card.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:45.440
But when Shadow Ghoul attacks you, it's all over.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.100
I'll pass this turn.

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:50.600
Swords of Revealing Light now vanishes.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:59.110
Swords of Revealing Light can no longer stop attacks.

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:00.810
I'll pass this turn.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.410
Then it's my turn.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:06.200
What are you waiting for?

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:07.970
It's a secret.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:16.220
Did you get the card that you were waiting for?

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:34.240
I surrender, Arthur.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.400
You win.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.280
I surrender.

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:52.740
Why, Yugi?

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:54.010
Why did you give up?

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.560
What's going on?

00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:59.380
I win!

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:01.400
Yes, I lose.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:05.970
Bravo!  I really am powerful, right Teddy?

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:08.140
I did it!

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:10.400
He didn't get the card he was waiting for?

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.410
You must be kidding, Yugi.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.710
Now give me Blue-Eyes.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:24.640
You tore my grandfather's cherished Blue-Eyes!

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:25.820
I'm sorry.

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:27.960
That's why you didn't want to return it!

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:31.070
Goddamn!  I'll never forgive you!

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.900
I was planning to return it, but...

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:36.400
I don't want to hear your excuses!

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:37.660
Stop, Rebecca.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.110
Grandfather?

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:43.320
Arthur, it's you!

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:46.380
It's been awhile, Sugoroku.

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:49.050
It truly has.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:53.480
My granddaughter is such a troublemaker.

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:55.050
Sorry about that.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:55.990
Grandfather?

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:59.570
Rebecca, Yugi won this duel.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.840
That's not true!

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:04.940
Yugi, that was a fine duel.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:08.230
You're an excellent duelist, just like Sugoroku.

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:11.870
I knew it.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:14.310
Rebecca, take a look.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:17.840
This card is Soul Release.

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:22.300
If Yugi played this card on the final turn...

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:29.990
Soul Release allows you to banish up to five cards from your graveyards.

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:35.430
If he used it, Shadow Ghoul's attack points would have dropped from 2800 to 2300.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:39.370
If it battled Dark Magician and its 2500 attack points...

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:45.280
Yugi surrendered on purpose?

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:46.170
Why?

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:48.720
You still don't know?

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:52.950
Yugi is a kindhearted boy, like Sugoroku.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:57.770
He wanted to save you from caring only about winning and losing.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:06.400
Just like how Sugoroku saved my life when we were trapped in the ruins and dueling for water.

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:12.130
I became incredibly weak.

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:18.700
You surrendered on purpose.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:22.040
Winning or losing isn't important, but your life is.

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.800
Sugoroku...

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:32.730
I found them!

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:33.480
Are you okay?

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:34.360
Are you alive?

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:35.050
Just wait!

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:51.060
Rebecca, I did discard one monster after another to the graveyard to power up Shadow Ghoul.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:55.810
However, you must honor those that you lost.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:19:01.500
That goes for dueling as well as archeology when I investigate ancient graveyards.

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:07.520
A duelist must never forget to respect her opponent.

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:13.960
I was so thankful that I gave my cherished Blue-Eyes to Sugoroku.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:17.630
But Sugoroku ripped that precious card!

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:20.980
I'm sorry, Arthur.  You see...

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:22.850
It's fine, Sugoroku.

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:26.120
You kept it instead of throwing it away.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:30.920
Even though that card may be torn, our friendship will never be torn apart.

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:35.870
Listen, Rebecca.  Cards are about heart.

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:39.850
And truly great duels create friendships.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.290
Heart?

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.020
Yes, heart.

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:46.800
If you can't understand that, you can't be the American champion.

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:49.890
Yugi, I...

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:51.560
It's fine, Rebecca.

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.170
Thank you, Yugi.

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.100
Rebecca, take this.

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:59.100
The Ties of Friendship?

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:01.180
Yeah.  I want you to have it.

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:02.060
Yugi!

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:06.460
Sugoroku, care to have a duel for old times' sake?

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:08.750
Sure!  I won't surrender this time!

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:11.750
This will be fun!  Do your best!

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:14.420
But Gramps, are you healthy enough to duel?

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:17.010
Yes!  I'm full of energy-  Ouch...

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:18.320
Grandpa!

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:19.860
Are you okay?

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:35.760
What?  Kaiba fell for The Big Five's trap and is stuck in an adventure game?

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:42.600
Mokuba, Yugi and Jonouchi enter a game world using virtual capsules to rescue Kaiba.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:48.700
Be careful!  If you don't beat the game, you can't return to the real world!

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:52.560
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Big 5's Trap
Duel Monsters Quest

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:54.560
Duel, standby!

00:20:59.510 --> 00:21:07.910
The flask glistens

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:15.760
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:24.740
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:32.510
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:38.340
Shower of happiness

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:42.460
I will shower you with it

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:50.730
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:54.970
Shower of happiness

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:59.090
You are not alone

00:21:59.470 --> 00:22:05.810
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
